1
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:49,850
Magnificent.

2
00:03:51,030 --> 00:03:52,670
Looks fresh-forged.

3
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,690
It is.

4
00:03:55,390 --> 00:03:57,170
No one's made a Valyrian steel sword

5
00:03:57,170 --> 00:03:58,710
since the Doom of Valyria.

6
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:02,820
There are three living smiths who know how to rework Valyrian steel.

7
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:05,820
The finest of them was in Volantis.

8
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:08,730
Came here to King's Landing at my invitation.

9
00:04:08,730 --> 00:04:10,730
Where did you get this much Valyrian steel?

10
00:04:10,730 --> 00:04:13,200
From someone who no longer had need of it.

11
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:18,690
You've wanted one of these in the family for a long time.

12
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:20,700
-And now we have two.  -Two?

13
00:04:20,710 --> 00:04:23,180
The original weapon was absurdly large.

14
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:25,580
Plenty of steel for two swords.

15
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:27,750
Well, thank you. It's glorious.

16
00:04:34,790 --> 00:04:36,570
You'll have to train your left hand.

17
00:04:36,570 --> 00:04:38,990
Any decent swordsman knows how to use both hands.

18
00:04:38,990 --> 00:04:40,430
You'll never be as good.

19
00:04:41,410 --> 00:04:42,400
No.

20
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,420
But as long as I'm better than everyone else,

21
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:45,860
I suppose it doesn't matter.

22
00:04:46,810 --> 00:04:49,610
You can't serve in the Kingsguard with one hand.

23
00:04:49,610 --> 00:04:52,010
Where's that written? I can and I will.

24
00:04:52,010 --> 00:04:53,180
The Kingsguard oath is for life.

25
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:54,950
The war is over. The king is safe.

26
00:04:54,950 --> 00:04:56,710
The king is never safe.

27
00:04:57,020 --> 00:04:58,430
How many people in this city alone

28
00:04:58,430 --> 00:04:59,870
would love to see his head on a pike?

29
00:04:59,870 --> 00:05:02,010
Other knights protected the king while you were a prisoner.

30
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:05,290
They will continue to do so when you go home.

31
00:05:05,770 --> 00:05:08,850
-Home?  -You'll return to Casterly Rock

32
00:05:08,850 --> 00:05:10,610
and rule in my stead.

33
00:05:10,610 --> 00:05:13,220
You are the Lord of Casterly Rock.

34
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:17,690
I am the King's Hand. My place is here.

35
00:05:18,030 --> 00:05:20,980
I don't expect to see the Rock again before I die.

36
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:23,370
You know what they call me?

37
00:05:24,330 --> 00:05:25,960
Kingslayer. Oathbreaker.

38
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:27,570
Man without honor.

39
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:30,040
Now you want me to break another sacred vow.

40
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:32,810
You won't be breaking anything.

41
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:35,900
There is a precedent to relieve a Kingsguard of his duties.

42
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:38,830
The king will exercise that prerogative.

43
00:05:39,410 --> 00:05:41,800
-No.  -No?

44
00:05:42,670 --> 00:05:43,640
No.

45
00:05:45,430 --> 00:05:47,120
I don't believe I asked you a question.

46
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,440
There's my answer.

47
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:49,860
If you think your bloody honor comes before your family.

48
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:52,130
My bloody honor is beyond repair,

49
00:05:52,130 --> 00:05:54,360
but my answer is still no. I don't want Casterly Rock.

50
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:56,220
I don't want a wife. I don't want children.

51
00:05:56,220 --> 00:05:57,620
What do you want?

52
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:01,010
Supper would be nice.

53
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:05,100
For 40 years I've tried to teach you.

54
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:08,070
If you haven't learned by now, you never will.

55
00:06:09,010 --> 00:06:09,900
Go.

56
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:13,140
If serving as a glorified bodyguard is the sum of your ambition,

57
00:06:13,140 --> 00:06:14,810
go serve.

58
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,700
I suppose you want the sword back.

59
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:18,920
Keep it.

60
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:23,160
A one-handed man with no family needs all the help he can get.

61
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:53,400
How many Dornishmen does it take to fuck a goat?

62
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:54,410
Please don't.

63
00:06:56,600 --> 00:07:00,500
Seems to me, the smart place to meet travelers is in a tavern.

64
00:07:00,610 --> 00:07:02,410
That way, one party is late,

65
00:07:02,410 --> 00:07:04,870
the other party can drink some ale inside.

66
00:07:04,870 --> 00:07:06,490
This is the Prince of Dorne we're waiting for,

67
00:07:06,490 --> 00:07:08,820
not one of your sellsword friends.

68
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:12,250
If he's so damned important, how come they sent you to meet him?

69
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:17,430
There's bad blood between the Martells of Dorne

70
00:07:17,430 --> 00:07:20,280
and the Lannisters of Casterly Rock. Has been for years.

71
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:22,610
And just in case the Martells of Dorne

72
00:07:22,610 --> 00:07:24,390
are looking to spill some Lannister blood,

73
00:07:24,390 --> 00:07:26,440
-it may as well be yours, eh?  -No need for cynicism.

74
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:28,620
I happen to be an accomplished diplomat.

75
00:07:29,910 --> 00:07:32,280
Ah, here we are.

76
00:07:35,770 --> 00:07:37,140
Can you read the sigils?

77
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:40,650
Yellow balls?

78
00:07:40,650 --> 00:07:42,520
Wild lemons on a purple field,

79
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:44,130
House Dalt of Lemonwood.

80
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:49,430
A vulture grasping a baby in its talons, House Blackmont.

81
00:07:49,430 --> 00:07:52,030
A crowned skull, the Manwoodys of Kingsgrave.

82
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:53,760
Boy knows his Dornish Houses.

83
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:55,110
I need a sigil.

84
00:07:55,110 --> 00:07:58,270
And House Martell, a red sun pierced by a spear?

85
00:07:59,350 --> 00:08:00,710
I don't see it, my lord.

86
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:05,650
Well met, my lords.

87
00:08:05,650 --> 00:08:08,190
His Grace King Joffrey welcomes you in his name.

88
00:08:08,190 --> 00:08:11,330
My lord father, the King's Hand, sends his greetings as well.

89
00:08:11,330 --> 00:08:14,550
I am Tyrion Lannister of Casterly Rock, master of Coin.

90
00:08:18,670 --> 00:08:19,610
Forgive me.

91
00:08:20,410 --> 00:08:22,730
I don't see Prince Doran in your company.

92
00:08:22,730 --> 00:08:26,580
The prince's health forces him to remain at Sunspear.

93
00:08:27,330 --> 00:08:30,030
He sends his brother Prince Oberyn

94
00:08:30,030 --> 00:08:32,130
to attend the royal wedding in his stead.

95
00:08:34,670 --> 00:08:38,990
Yes, the king will be delighted to enjoy the company of a warrior

96
00:08:38,990 --> 00:08:41,920
as renowned as Prince Oberyn at his wedding feast.

97
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:42,760
Will he?

98
00:08:44,350 --> 00:08:45,850
And where is Prince Oberyn?

99
00:08:45,970 --> 00:08:47,460
Arrived before dawn.

100
00:08:48,010 --> 00:08:51,020
Not a man for welcome parties, our prince.

101
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:55,690
Very well. My lords, these fine men from the City Watch

102
00:08:55,690 --> 00:08:58,530
will escort you to your quarters in the Red Keep.

103
00:08:58,530 --> 00:09:01,360
You must be weary after such a long journey.

104
00:09:06,310 --> 00:09:08,170
Some accomplished diplomacy that was.

105
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:10,140
Now where?

106
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:12,700
We must find Prince Oberyn before he kills somebody

107
00:09:12,710 --> 00:09:14,390
or several somebodies.

108
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:17,400
How do you plan on finding a single Dornishman in a city this big?

109
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:19,550
You're famous for fucking half of Westeros.

110
00:09:19,550 --> 00:09:22,330
You just arrived at the capital after two weeks of bad roads,

111
00:09:22,330 --> 00:09:23,740
where would you go?

112
00:09:23,740 --> 00:09:26,890
I'd probably go to sleep, but I'm getting old.

113
00:09:51,450 --> 00:09:52,860
Look at this one.

114
00:09:55,110 --> 00:09:56,360
How lovely is she?

115
00:09:56,910 --> 00:09:57,980
Beautiful.

116
00:09:59,050 --> 00:10:00,390
But pale.

117
00:10:00,630 --> 00:10:02,240
They like them pale in the capital.

118
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:04,340
Shows they don't work the fields.

119
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:08,910
Do I frighten you?

120
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:12,580
You like?

121
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:15,970
Timid. Timid bores me.

122
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:24,450
You're a bit of mischief, aren't you?

123
00:10:27,070 --> 00:10:28,590
I think she likes you.

124
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:30,280
She has good taste.

125
00:10:33,090 --> 00:10:34,630
You're not timid, are you?

126
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:41,570
Not timid.

127
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:43,420
Do you like women?

128
00:10:44,090 --> 00:10:45,530
When they look like her, my lord.

129
00:10:45,530 --> 00:10:47,760
This one will do nicely.

130
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:49,570
Very good, my lady.

131
00:10:49,970 --> 00:10:51,840
Oh, I'm not a lady.

132
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:54,290
A term of courtesy in this establishment.

133
00:10:54,290 --> 00:10:56,190
A lie anywhere.

134
00:10:56,750 --> 00:10:58,500
Why not use the right words?

135
00:10:58,810 --> 00:11:00,140
I'm a bastard.

136
00:11:00,610 --> 00:11:03,760
She is a whore. And you're what?

137
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:05,650
A procurer.

138
00:11:06,870 --> 00:11:08,010
Any of the others?

139
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:11,680
The two girls can leave.

140
00:11:12,780 --> 00:11:13,760
You stay.

141
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:17,060
I'm afraid I'm not an offer, my lord.

142
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:19,310
Everyone who works for Littlefinger is an offer.

143
00:11:20,810 --> 00:11:23,120
Take off your clothes. We'll be here a while.

144
00:11:23,130 --> 00:11:25,960
-My lord.  -I am a prince, boy.

145
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:29,360
Have you ever been with a prince?

146
00:11:30,790 --> 00:11:32,120
Can't say I have.

147
00:11:35,870 --> 00:11:37,630
I'm wildly expensive.

148
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:41,810
Take off your clothes.

149
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:50,660
Which way do you like it?

150
00:11:53,730 --> 00:11:54,730
My way.

151
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:06,520
Oberyn.

152
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:09,580
Oberyn, don't.

153
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:18,240
Yes, not the rains weep o'er his hall,

154
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:24,260
and not a soul to hear.

155
00:12:32,490 --> 00:12:33,580
You lost, friend?

156
00:12:33,890 --> 00:12:35,450
Forgive me for staring.

157
00:12:36,970 --> 00:12:39,380
I don't see many Lannisters where I'm from.

158
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:42,120
I don't see many Dornishmen in the capital.

159
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:43,440
We don't like the smell.

160
00:12:45,470 --> 00:12:48,070
-Come with me, lover.  -Gods, look at this one.

161
00:12:48,070 --> 00:12:50,030
Sirs, if you follow me, I'll arrange for a private room.

162
00:12:50,030 --> 00:12:52,820
Why are you wasting a woman like this on a Dornishman?

163
00:12:52,820 --> 00:12:54,920
Bring him a shaved goat and a bottle of olive oil.

164
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:02,930
Do you know why all the world hates a Lannister?

165
00:13:08,920 --> 00:13:12,690
You think your gold and your lions

166
00:13:12,690 --> 00:13:15,880
and your gold lions make you better than everyone.

167
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:19,740
May I tell you a secret?

168
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:22,680
You're not a golden lion.

169
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:25,870
You're just a pink little man

170
00:13:25,870 --> 00:13:28,250
who is far too slow on the draw.

171
00:13:37,090 --> 00:13:40,640
Longsword is a bad option in close quarters.

172
00:13:40,780 --> 00:13:42,860
When I pull my blade, your friend starts bleeding.

173
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:45,920
Quite a lot, I'm afraid. So many veins in the wrist.

174
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:49,650
He'll live if you get him help straightaway.

175
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:54,660
So, decisions.

176
00:13:56,470 --> 00:13:58,000
Prince Oberyn, forgive the intrusion.

177
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,420
We heard there might be

178
00:14:00,410 --> 00:14:01,180
trouble.

179
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:04,930
Apologies, my love.

180
00:14:11,150 --> 00:14:13,180
I'm here to welcome you to the capital.

181
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:20,700
Ellaria Sand, my paramour.

182
00:14:21,870 --> 00:14:23,550
The king's own Uncle Imp.

183
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:26,840
Tyrion, son of Tywin Lannister.

184
00:14:26,970 --> 00:14:28,960
If there's anything I can do to make your stay.

185
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:30,750
What are you? His hired killer?

186
00:14:30,780 --> 00:14:33,760
It started that way, aye. Now I'm a knight.

187
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:35,320
How did that come to pass?

188
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,790
Killed the right people, I suppose.

189
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:44,790
We'll need a few more girls. Girls, yes?

190
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:46,570
You don't partake?

191
00:14:46,570 --> 00:14:48,720
Oh, I partook. Now I'm married.

192
00:14:49,610 --> 00:14:52,230
Prince Oberyn, if I may, a word in private?

193
00:14:57,350 --> 00:14:59,570
Seems I visited the Lannister brothel by mistake.

194
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:02,120
-Oh, they take all kinds.  -Even Dornishmen.

195
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:04,480
The king is very grateful that you traveled all

196
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:05,690
this way for his wedding.

197
00:15:05,690 --> 00:15:08,830
Let us speak truth here. Joffrey is insulted.

198
00:15:09,420 --> 00:15:11,770
I am only the second son after all.

199
00:15:11,770 --> 00:15:14,100
Well, speaking as a fellow second son,

200
00:15:14,210 --> 00:15:17,350
I have grown rather used to being the family insult.

201
00:15:18,610 --> 00:15:20,990
Why did you come to King's Landing, Prince Oberyn?

202
00:15:20,990 --> 00:15:22,680
I was invited to the royal wedding.

203
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:24,590
I thought we were speaking truth.

204
00:15:26,090 --> 00:15:29,080
The last time I was in the capital was many years ago.

205
00:15:29,370 --> 00:15:30,440
Another wedding.

206
00:15:31,710 --> 00:15:33,150
My sister Elia

207
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:36,520
and Rhaegar Targaryen, the Last Dragon.

208
00:15:39,510 --> 00:15:42,860
My sister loved him. She bore his children.

209
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:46,280
Swaddled them, rocked them, fed them at her own breast.

210
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:48,560
Elia wouldn't let the wet nurse touch them.

211
00:15:49,690 --> 00:15:52,420
And beautiful, noble Rhaegar Targaryen

212
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:55,680
left her for another woman.

213
00:15:57,020 --> 00:15:58,140
That started a war

214
00:15:58,140 --> 00:16:00,150
and the war ended right here,

215
00:16:01,030 --> 00:16:03,230
when your father's army took the city.

216
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:04,550
I wasn't actually present.

217
00:16:04,550 --> 00:16:06,400
And butchered those children.

218
00:16:08,780 --> 00:16:10,410
My nephew and niece.

219
00:16:10,770 --> 00:16:14,260
Carved them up and wrapped them in Lannister cloaks.

220
00:16:16,700 --> 00:16:19,560
And my sister, you know what they did to her?

221
00:16:23,100 --> 00:16:24,420
I'm asking you a question.

222
00:16:24,420 --> 00:16:26,040
I've heard rumors.

223
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:28,420
So have I.

224
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:33,100
The one I keep hearing is that Gregor Clegane the Mountain

225
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:36,120
raped Elia and split her in half

226
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,540
with his great sword.

227
00:16:37,540 --> 00:16:39,310
I wasn't there. I don't know what happened.

228
00:16:39,310 --> 00:16:40,990
If the Mountain killed my sister,

229
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,980
your father gave the order.

230
00:16:44,410 --> 00:16:45,940
Tell your father, I'm here.

231
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:49,690
And tell him the Lannisters

232
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:51,900
aren't the only ones who pay their debts.

233
00:18:14,670 --> 00:18:16,310
They're dragons, Khaleesi.

234
00:18:17,180 --> 00:18:18,790
They can never be tamed.

235
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:21,390
Not even by their mother.

236
00:18:43,030 --> 00:18:45,480
-Ser Barristan.  -Your Grace.

237
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:48,690
Where's Daario Naharis?

238
00:18:48,970 --> 00:18:50,180
Where's Grey Worm?

239
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:54,250
Gambling, Your Grace.

240
00:18:56,030 --> 00:18:57,100
Gambling?

241
00:19:19,790 --> 00:19:23,120
Mhysa. Mhysa. Mhysa.

242
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:26,220
Mhysa. Mhysa. Mhysa.

243
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:31,100
Mhysa. Mhysa. Mhysa.

244
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:33,230
How long have they been at it?

245
00:19:33,650 --> 00:19:35,420
Since midnight, Your Grace.

246
00:19:36,410 --> 00:19:38,470
Ser Worm is stronger than he looks.

247
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:40,290
But I can see his arms beginning to shake.

248
00:19:40,290 --> 00:19:42,740
What's the prize to winning this stupid contest?

249
00:19:42,740 --> 00:19:45,160
The honor of riding by your side on the road to Meereen.

250
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:48,260
That honor goes to Ser Jorah and Ser Barristan

251
00:19:48,260 --> 00:19:50,940
as neither of them kept me waiting this morning.

252
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:54,490
You two will ride in the rear guard and protect the livestock.

253
00:19:56,350 --> 00:19:58,150
The last man holding his sword

254
00:19:58,150 --> 00:20:00,230
can find a new queen to fight for.

255
00:20:29,820 --> 00:20:31,530
You need to eat something.

256
00:20:35,140 --> 00:20:36,290
Pigeon pie.

257
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:38,710
No, thank you.

258
00:20:43,020 --> 00:20:44,280
Lemon cakes?

259
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:46,880
No, thank you.

260
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:48,670
You love lemon cakes.

261
00:20:50,190 --> 00:20:51,730
Tell her, she needs to eat.

262
00:20:51,730 --> 00:20:53,600
My lady, you do need to eat.

263
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:55,280
I don't need to eat.

264
00:20:57,860 --> 00:21:00,510
If I could have a moment alone with my wife.

265
00:21:09,930 --> 00:21:11,390
She needs to eat.

266
00:21:18,770 --> 00:21:20,750
I can't let you starve.

267
00:21:21,330 --> 00:21:22,960
I swore to protect you.

268
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:30,900
My lady,

269
00:21:32,270 --> 00:21:34,620
I am your husband. Let me help you.

270
00:21:36,510 --> 00:21:38,260
How can you help me?

271
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:40,830
I don't know, but I can try.

272
00:21:42,540 --> 00:21:46,840
I lie awake all night staring at the canopy

273
00:21:47,810 --> 00:21:50,120
thinking about how they died.

274
00:21:50,450 --> 00:21:53,410
I could get you essence of nightshade to help you sleep.

275
00:21:53,410 --> 00:21:55,380
Do you know what they did to my brother?

276
00:21:57,230 --> 00:22:00,620
How they sewed his direwolf's head onto his body?

277
00:22:02,300 --> 00:22:03,620
And my mother.

278
00:22:04,540 --> 00:22:06,910
They say they cut her throat to the bone

279
00:22:06,910 --> 00:22:09,010
and threw her body in the river.

280
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:12,650
What happened to your family was a terrible crime.

281
00:22:13,980 --> 00:22:15,180
I didn't know your brother.

282
00:22:15,180 --> 00:22:17,630
He seemed like a good man, but I didn't know him.

283
00:22:18,830 --> 00:22:20,720
Your mother, on the other hand,

284
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:22,150
I admired her.

285
00:22:22,900 --> 00:22:24,360
She wanted to have me executed,

286
00:22:24,360 --> 00:22:25,740
but I admired her.

287
00:22:28,260 --> 00:22:29,850
She was a strong woman.

288
00:22:31,530 --> 00:22:34,710
And she was fierce when it came to protecting her children.

289
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:38,190
Sansa.

290
00:22:41,710 --> 00:22:43,730
Your mother would want you to carry on.

291
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:45,190
You know it's true.

292
00:22:50,410 --> 00:22:51,730
Will you pardon me, my lord?

293
00:22:51,730 --> 00:22:53,180
I'd like to visit the godswood.

294
00:22:53,180 --> 00:22:56,160
Of course. Of course. Prayer can be helpful, I hear.

295
00:22:57,170 --> 00:22:58,680
I don't pray anymore.

296
00:22:59,560 --> 00:23:02,660
It's the only place I can go where people don't talk to me.

297
00:23:21,370 --> 00:23:22,700
My lion.

298
00:23:24,320 --> 00:23:25,770
What are you doing?

299
00:23:28,620 --> 00:23:30,380
What does it look like I'm doing?

300
00:23:31,740 --> 00:23:32,340
Come here.

301
00:23:32,340 --> 00:23:34,630
How many times have I told you? You can't visit me here.

302
00:23:34,630 --> 00:23:36,430
I know. I know.

303
00:23:36,430 --> 00:23:38,790
We have come to a dangerous place.

304
00:23:39,220 --> 00:23:41,750
Have you forgotten me? Do you know how long it's been?

305
00:23:41,750 --> 00:23:43,240
Of course I haven't forgotten.

306
00:23:43,240 --> 00:23:45,250
I want you.

307
00:23:45,580 --> 00:23:46,940
Don't you want me?

308
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:50,720
Things are a bit tense right now.

309
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:52,200
What things?

310
00:23:53,070 --> 00:23:55,150
My nephew the king wants to murder me.

311
00:23:55,300 --> 00:23:57,910
My wife hates me, because my father murdered her family.

312
00:23:57,910 --> 00:23:59,600
Oberyn Martell wants to murder everyone

313
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:01,160
whose last name is Lannister.

314
00:24:01,970 --> 00:24:05,720
You need to relax.

315
00:24:15,030 --> 00:24:16,700
Don't you want to relax?

316
00:24:22,050 --> 00:24:23,920
-What's wrong?  -I told you.

317
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:26,670
-It's not a good time.  -It's never a good time.

318
00:24:27,120 --> 00:24:29,590
-You have your child bride now.  -Shae.

319
00:24:30,380 --> 00:24:32,220
-Do you love her?  -Love her?

320
00:24:32,410 --> 00:24:34,290
I barely know her. She's a child.

321
00:24:34,290 --> 00:24:37,120
-She despises me.  -That's not an answer.

322
00:24:37,120 --> 00:24:38,290
Of course I don't love her.

323
00:24:39,710 --> 00:24:41,050
You tried to ship me away.

324
00:24:41,860 --> 00:24:43,100
Ship you away?

325
00:24:45,090 --> 00:24:47,450
Give me diamonds and make me disappear.

326
00:24:47,450 --> 00:24:48,830
What in the world are you talking about?

327
00:24:48,830 --> 00:24:50,880
If you want me to leave, just say it.

328
00:24:52,650 --> 00:24:54,290
Say it!

329
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:57,140
I don't know what you're talking about.

330
00:24:58,340 --> 00:24:59,650
You want me to stay?

331
00:25:27,920 --> 00:25:29,640
A work of art, really.

332
00:25:30,840 --> 00:25:32,790
The craftsmanship is excellent.

333
00:25:32,800 --> 00:25:33,590
You like it so much,

334
00:25:33,590 --> 00:25:35,410
you're welcome to chop off your own hand and take it.

335
00:25:35,410 --> 00:25:37,670
Such an ingrate. I spent days with the goldsmith

336
00:25:37,670 --> 00:25:39,040
getting the details just right.

337
00:25:39,240 --> 00:25:40,540
Days?

338
00:25:41,320 --> 00:25:42,820
Better part of an afternoon.

339
00:25:43,420 --> 00:25:45,070
There, how does that feel?

340
00:25:48,140 --> 00:25:49,940
a hook would be more practical.

341
00:25:49,940 --> 00:25:51,540
Elegant, I think.

342
00:25:57,520 --> 00:25:58,970
Thank you for your help with the other matter.

343
00:25:58,970 --> 00:26:01,330
-The symptoms have abated?  -Gone completely.

344
00:26:01,330 --> 00:26:02,890
I am in your debt, Maester Qyburn.

345
00:26:02,890 --> 00:26:06,420
Not a maester, Your Grace, but happy to help whenever I can.

346
00:26:16,610 --> 00:26:17,630
Odd little man.

347
00:26:17,630 --> 00:26:19,190
I've grown rather fond of him.

348
00:26:19,810 --> 00:26:21,300
He's quite talented, you know?

349
00:26:21,590 --> 00:26:22,930
What symptoms?

350
00:26:23,910 --> 00:26:26,000
Symptoms that are not your concern.

351
00:26:26,230 --> 00:26:27,500
You let him touch you?

352
00:26:28,460 --> 00:26:29,390
You jealous?

353
00:26:30,410 --> 00:26:31,750
I'm surprised.

354
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:33,680
You never let Pycelle near you.

355
00:26:34,080 --> 00:26:36,640
You think I'd let that old lecher put his hands on me?

356
00:26:38,850 --> 00:26:40,480
He smells like a dead cat.

357
00:26:40,490 --> 00:26:42,780
I'm not sure I've ever smelled a dead cat.

358
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:44,820
Well, they smell like Pycelle.

359
00:26:45,200 --> 00:26:46,800
You drink more than you used to.

360
00:26:48,290 --> 00:26:50,070
-Yes.  -Why?

361
00:26:50,080 --> 00:26:54,120
Let's see, you started a brawl in the streets with Ned Stark

362
00:26:54,130 --> 00:26:55,690
and disappeared from the capital.

363
00:26:56,230 --> 00:26:58,920
My husband died in a tragic hunting accident.

364
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:00,450
It must have been traumatic for you.

365
00:27:00,450 --> 00:27:02,230
My only daughter was shipped off to Dorne.

366
00:27:02,230 --> 00:27:03,580
We suffered through a siege.

367
00:27:03,580 --> 00:27:04,880
A rather short siege.

368
00:27:04,880 --> 00:27:07,710
A rather short siege that I didn't expect to survive.

369
00:27:07,710 --> 00:27:09,470
And now, I'm marrying my eldest son

370
00:27:09,470 --> 00:27:12,110
to a wicked little bitch from Highgarden,

371
00:27:12,430 --> 00:27:13,980
while I'm supposed to marry her brother,

372
00:27:13,980 --> 00:27:15,810
a renowned pillow biter. So.

373
00:27:16,790 --> 00:27:18,600
Father disowned me today.

374
00:27:19,350 --> 00:27:21,620
He can't disown you. You're all he's got.

375
00:27:21,770 --> 00:27:23,390
You're forgetting Tyrion.

376
00:27:24,510 --> 00:27:27,780
You don't really plan on staying in the Kingsguard, do you?

377
00:27:32,040 --> 00:27:35,480
Staying in the Kingsguard means I live right here

378
00:27:35,600 --> 00:27:37,700
in the Red Keep with you.

379
00:27:39,400 --> 00:27:40,820
-Not now.  -I want.

380
00:27:41,180 --> 00:27:44,280
Not now? When? I've been back for weeks.

381
00:27:48,530 --> 00:27:51,320
-Something's changed.  -Everything's changed.

382
00:27:51,680 --> 00:27:53,950
You come back after all this time with no apologies

383
00:27:53,950 --> 00:27:56,750
and one hand and expect everything to be the same?

384
00:27:56,750 --> 00:27:58,110
What do you want me to apologize for?

385
00:27:58,110 --> 00:27:58,980
For leaving me.

386
00:27:58,980 --> 00:28:00,740
You think I wanted to be taken prisoner?

387
00:28:00,740 --> 00:28:02,480
Don't know what you wanted. You weren't here.

388
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:06,300
You left me alone.

389
00:28:06,300 --> 00:28:09,100
Every day I was a prisoner, I plotted my escape.

390
00:28:09,100 --> 00:28:12,400
Every day. I murdered people so I could be here with you.

391
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:14,190
-You took too long.  -I.

392
00:28:16,290 --> 00:28:19,220
-What are you saying?  -I'm saying you took too long.

393
00:28:20,060 --> 00:28:21,360
-Come in.  -Go away.

394
00:28:23,070 --> 00:28:24,510
Forgive me, Your Grace.

395
00:28:25,490 --> 00:28:28,240
You told me to come at once if there was anything important.

396
00:28:48,360 --> 00:28:50,920
You plan on killing all the crows yourself?

397
00:28:52,820 --> 00:28:55,670
Do you plan on sitting here scratching your balls till winter?

398
00:28:55,920 --> 00:28:57,530
We wait for Mance's orders.

399
00:28:57,530 --> 00:28:59,820
You sent a man over the Wall at the full moon.

400
00:28:59,820 --> 00:29:01,780
If he's not back yet, he's not coming back.

401
00:29:01,780 --> 00:29:03,280
And what is it you want?

402
00:29:03,280 --> 00:29:05,690
March on Castle Black with just this lot?

403
00:29:06,080 --> 00:29:08,770
Your pretty crow said 1,000 men are nesting there.

404
00:29:08,770 --> 00:29:10,060
Yeah, well, he's a liar.

405
00:29:10,060 --> 00:29:11,180
He is?

406
00:29:12,180 --> 00:29:14,650
Shouldn't it be "he was"?

407
00:29:15,370 --> 00:29:17,250
You said you put three arrows in him.

408
00:29:17,250 --> 00:29:18,340
I did.

409
00:29:18,750 --> 00:29:22,720
I've seen you slip a shaft through a rabbit's eye at 200 yards.

410
00:29:22,720 --> 00:29:27,220
If that boy's still walking, it's 'cause you let him go.

411
00:29:51,730 --> 00:29:53,000
Thenns.

412
00:29:54,310 --> 00:29:56,610
I fucking hate Thenns.

413
00:30:07,110 --> 00:30:08,400
Mance sent you?

414
00:30:09,450 --> 00:30:10,970
How did you find us?

415
00:30:15,600 --> 00:30:18,960
You came from the south, not the north.

416
00:30:19,020 --> 00:30:20,580
Took a detour.

417
00:30:21,010 --> 00:30:23,950
Got some supper from a village down that way.

418
00:30:25,500 --> 00:30:29,080
Why does the meat down here taste so much better

419
00:30:29,080 --> 00:30:31,590
than it does on our side of the Wall?

420
00:30:31,630 --> 00:30:33,360
Help yourself.

421
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:38,740
Maybe everything's just better fed down here.

422
00:30:39,050 --> 00:30:41,510
Fat and lazy.

423
00:30:42,710 --> 00:30:45,050
Easier for us, hmm?

424
00:30:47,150 --> 00:30:48,900
You didn't see us coming?

425
00:30:49,790 --> 00:30:51,240
Lost your warg?

426
00:30:53,510 --> 00:30:55,980
And that baby crow you had with you,

427
00:30:57,360 --> 00:30:58,800
lost him too?

428
00:31:01,070 --> 00:31:02,940
I'll answer to Mance.

429
00:31:03,350 --> 00:31:05,240
I won't answer to you.

430
00:31:06,320 --> 00:31:07,790
She yours?

431
00:31:10,210 --> 00:31:11,770
I'm not anybody's.

432
00:31:21,430 --> 00:31:23,130
Too scrawny.

433
00:31:23,810 --> 00:31:26,860
Not like those crows at Castle Black.

434
00:31:27,410 --> 00:31:30,470
Think of them stuck in their larders

435
00:31:30,520 --> 00:31:34,210
stuffing their faces with ham and blood sausage

436
00:31:34,210 --> 00:31:37,610
and stew, getting nice and fat

437
00:31:37,610 --> 00:31:39,320
and marbled.

438
00:31:40,090 --> 00:31:43,210
I know we've had our differences, Tormund,

439
00:31:43,630 --> 00:31:47,560
but just one time before you die,

440
00:31:47,750 --> 00:31:51,340
you really ought to try crow.

441
00:31:53,940 --> 00:31:55,020
Draw.

442
00:31:56,100 --> 00:31:57,130
Loose.

443
00:32:04,840 --> 00:32:06,210
Last time I saw him,

444
00:32:06,210 --> 00:32:08,120
he was in the courtyard at Winterfell.

445
00:32:10,910 --> 00:32:12,810
He said, "Next time I see you,

446
00:32:13,560 --> 00:32:15,240
you'll be all in black."

447
00:32:18,350 --> 00:32:20,610
I was jealous of Robb my whole life.

448
00:32:22,480 --> 00:32:24,110
The way my father looked at him,

449
00:32:24,220 --> 00:32:25,610
I wanted that.

450
00:32:26,890 --> 00:32:28,900
He was better than me at everything,

451
00:32:31,120 --> 00:32:33,880
fighting and hunting,

452
00:32:34,290 --> 00:32:35,680
and riding,

453
00:32:36,930 --> 00:32:38,260
and girls.

454
00:32:38,820 --> 00:32:40,600
Gods, the girls loved him.

455
00:32:42,380 --> 00:32:45,720
I wanted to hate him, but I never could.

456
00:32:48,500 --> 00:32:50,640
Sometimes I want to hate you.

457
00:32:53,230 --> 00:32:56,480
Well, you're better than me at everything.

458
00:32:58,890 --> 00:33:00,250
Except reading.

459
00:33:02,910 --> 00:33:06,710
They're ready for you.

460
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:13,610
He's wanted to hang me for a while. Now's his chance.

461
00:33:13,610 --> 00:33:16,050
No one's going to hang you. You've done nothing wrong.

462
00:33:17,110 --> 00:33:18,880
I've done plenty wrong.

463
00:33:20,130 --> 00:33:23,230
So you admit you murdered Qhorin Halfhand?

464
00:33:24,200 --> 00:33:25,550
I didn't murder him.

465
00:33:25,550 --> 00:33:28,130
No? You put your sword

466
00:33:28,130 --> 00:33:30,130
through a brother of the Night's Watch.

467
00:33:30,130 --> 00:33:31,670
What do you call that?

468
00:33:32,490 --> 00:33:34,090
He wanted me to kill him.

469
00:33:34,270 --> 00:33:36,200
A bastard son of a traitor.

470
00:33:36,200 --> 00:33:37,700
What would you expect?

471
00:33:37,700 --> 00:33:39,330
The Halfhand believed our only chance

472
00:33:39,330 --> 00:33:41,910
to stop Mance was to get a man inside his army.

473
00:33:41,910 --> 00:33:44,360
Don't talk about the Halfhand as if you knew him.

474
00:33:44,510 --> 00:33:45,610
He was my brother.

475
00:33:45,610 --> 00:33:47,900
Then you'd know he'd do anything to defend the Wall.

476
00:33:47,920 --> 00:33:49,720
The free folk would have boiled him alive,

477
00:33:49,720 --> 00:33:50,760
but letting me kill him.

478
00:33:50,760 --> 00:33:53,080
The free folk? Listen to him.

479
00:33:53,280 --> 00:33:55,250
He even talks like a wildling now.

480
00:33:55,250 --> 00:33:58,120
Aye, I talk like a wildling. I ate with the wildlings.

481
00:33:58,120 --> 00:34:00,330
I climbed the Wall with the wildlings.

482
00:34:02,810 --> 00:34:04,760
I laid with a wildling girl.

483
00:34:06,980 --> 00:34:09,200
You admit to breaking your vows, then?

484
00:34:10,260 --> 00:34:11,360
I do.

485
00:34:12,020 --> 00:34:15,300
The law is the law. The boy must die.

486
00:34:15,370 --> 00:34:19,560
If we beheaded every ranger who lay with a girl,

487
00:34:19,580 --> 00:34:23,190
the Wall would be manned by headless men.

488
00:34:23,190 --> 00:34:25,400
There's a difference between sneaking off

489
00:34:25,410 --> 00:34:29,290
to the Mole's Town brothel and sleeping with the enemy.

490
00:34:30,120 --> 00:34:31,630
While we sit here

491
00:34:31,630 --> 00:34:33,840
debating which rules I broke,

492
00:34:34,320 --> 00:34:38,080
Mance Rayder marches on the Wall with an army of 100,000.

493
00:34:38,080 --> 00:34:39,450
Impossible.

494
00:34:39,450 --> 00:34:41,440
You can't get 50 wildlings together

495
00:34:41,440 --> 00:34:43,010
before they start killing each other.

496
00:34:43,010 --> 00:34:46,130
100,000. He's united the Thenns,

497
00:34:46,130 --> 00:34:47,920
the Hornfoots, the ice-river clans.

498
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:49,440
He has giants fighting for him.

499
00:34:49,440 --> 00:34:50,620
Giants?

500
00:34:52,820 --> 00:34:54,930
Have you ever been beyond the Wall, ser?

501
00:34:54,930 --> 00:34:57,490
I commanded the City Watch of King's Landing, boy.

502
00:34:57,500 --> 00:34:58,700
And now you're here.

503
00:34:58,710 --> 00:35:00,450
You must not have been very good at your job.

504
00:35:00,540 --> 00:35:01,770
How dare you?!

505
00:35:01,770 --> 00:35:04,380
There's a band of wildlings south of the Wall already

506
00:35:04,480 --> 00:35:06,300
led by Tormund Giantsbane.

507
00:35:06,300 --> 00:35:08,240
I killed their warg and three others.

508
00:35:08,540 --> 00:35:10,350
They shot me full of arrows.

509
00:35:11,610 --> 00:35:14,250
Their orders are to attack Castle Black from the south

510
00:35:14,250 --> 00:35:16,140
when Mance hits it from the north.

511
00:35:16,730 --> 00:35:19,060
The signal for the attack will be a bonfire.

512
00:35:19,670 --> 00:35:22,910
Mance said it would be the greatest fire the North has ever seen.

513
00:35:23,370 --> 00:35:24,800
That's the truth.

514
00:35:25,500 --> 00:35:26,990
All the truth.

515
00:35:31,430 --> 00:35:35,310
Do you intend to execute me or am I free to go?

516
00:35:35,310 --> 00:35:36,950
None of us are free.

517
00:35:37,430 --> 00:35:39,390
We are men of the Night's Watch.

518
00:35:39,650 --> 00:35:43,700
But we won't be taking your head today, Jon Snow.

519
00:35:44,310 --> 00:35:45,320
Go on.

520
00:35:56,150 --> 00:35:58,710
I am acting commander here, Maester Aemon.

521
00:35:58,710 --> 00:35:59,920
Yes, you are.

522
00:35:59,920 --> 00:36:01,900
And I don't trust the bastard.

523
00:36:03,100 --> 00:36:05,090
He told the truth.

524
00:36:05,090 --> 00:36:07,510
And you always know when a man's telling a lie?

525
00:36:07,510 --> 00:36:10,220
How did you acquire this magical power?

526
00:36:11,790 --> 00:36:14,420
I grew up in King's Landing.

527
00:36:18,020 --> 00:36:19,890
No. No.

528
00:36:19,890 --> 00:36:22,120
You're a queen, not an ox.

529
00:36:23,210 --> 00:36:26,090
Your grandfather gave me a necklace

530
00:36:26,100 --> 00:36:29,210
just like this one for my 51st nameday.

531
00:36:31,140 --> 00:36:33,130
The wedding is in a fortnight, Grandmother.

532
00:36:33,130 --> 00:36:35,000
You can't say no to everything.

533
00:36:35,010 --> 00:36:37,880
Nonsense. My little dears.

534
00:36:37,880 --> 00:36:40,850
Go and speak to the jewelers of King's Landing.

535
00:36:40,850 --> 00:36:43,360
Tell them who you are, tell them who sent you.

536
00:36:43,360 --> 00:36:45,580
The one who brings me the best necklace

537
00:36:46,150 --> 00:36:48,360
will get to keep the next best.

538
00:36:52,410 --> 00:36:55,200
The Margaery Tyrell who walks into the sept

539
00:36:55,200 --> 00:36:59,090
a fortnight from now will inspire 1,000 songs.

540
00:36:59,240 --> 00:37:02,320
Now, how sad it will be if she's wearing rubbish like that.

541
00:37:02,330 --> 00:37:05,230
Perhaps I should just let Joffrey choose it for me.

542
00:37:05,240 --> 00:37:08,090
End up with a string of dead sparrow heads around my neck.

543
00:37:08,090 --> 00:37:11,510
You watch that. Even here, even with me.

544
00:37:14,050 --> 00:37:16,140
My word.

545
00:37:16,280 --> 00:37:18,540
My lady. My lady.

546
00:37:19,310 --> 00:37:21,340
Please pardon me for interrupting.

547
00:37:21,620 --> 00:37:23,230
My name is Brienne of Tarth.

548
00:37:23,230 --> 00:37:25,690
We know who you are. We've heard all about you.

549
00:37:25,750 --> 00:37:27,450
But hearing is one thing.

550
00:37:27,590 --> 00:37:30,510
Aren't you just marvelous?

551
00:37:30,590 --> 00:37:33,360
Absolutely singular.

552
00:37:33,850 --> 00:37:36,160
I hear you knocked my grandson into the dirt

553
00:37:36,160 --> 00:37:38,080
like the silly little boy he is.

554
00:37:39,300 --> 00:37:41,910
My lady, I know this is a very busy time for you,

555
00:37:42,240 --> 00:37:44,070
but if I could just have a moment.

556
00:37:45,710 --> 00:37:47,520
You dare not refuse.

557
00:37:50,180 --> 00:37:51,510
A shadow?

558
00:37:51,720 --> 00:37:54,180
A shadow with the face of Stannis Baratheon.

559
00:37:55,750 --> 00:37:59,730
I swear to you by all the gods, it was Stannis.

560
00:38:00,090 --> 00:38:02,560
He plunged his sword through Renly's heart

561
00:38:02,780 --> 00:38:04,310
and disappeared.

562
00:38:05,330 --> 00:38:07,710
One day, my lady, I will avenge our king.

563
00:38:07,940 --> 00:38:09,680
Joffrey is our king now.

564
00:38:11,110 --> 00:38:12,390
I meant no offense.

565
00:38:12,390 --> 00:38:13,850
And you've given none.

566
00:38:23,660 --> 00:38:25,910
All the Kingsguard will be on duty, of course.

567
00:38:25,910 --> 00:38:27,720
Ser Boros will be stationed here.

568
00:38:27,720 --> 00:38:29,700
Ser Preston will be stationed here

569
00:38:29,700 --> 00:38:33,270
beside the primary entertainment.

570
00:38:34,660 --> 00:38:35,880
Your Grace?

571
00:38:37,250 --> 00:38:39,260
Yes, yes, one guard at the,

572
00:38:39,260 --> 00:38:41,070
the thing. Go on.

573
00:38:41,070 --> 00:38:43,790
Ser Meryn will guard Lady Margaery and Tommen.

574
00:38:44,580 --> 00:38:47,230
I've always guarded the king himself, my lord.

575
00:38:47,480 --> 00:38:49,250
Ever since your absence.

576
00:38:49,250 --> 00:38:50,780
And I thank you for it, Ser Meryn.

577
00:38:50,780 --> 00:38:53,480
All very good. I don't expect any trouble.

578
00:38:54,510 --> 00:38:56,020
The people love their king.

579
00:38:56,020 --> 00:38:57,490
They know who keeps them fed.

580
00:38:57,490 --> 00:38:59,460
Margaery Tyrell, I've heard.

581
00:39:00,760 --> 00:39:02,590
By my leave.

582
00:39:02,590 --> 00:39:04,370
They know I saved the city.

583
00:39:04,370 --> 00:39:05,510
They know I won the war.

584
00:39:05,510 --> 00:39:07,790
The war's not won. Not while Stannis lives.

585
00:39:07,790 --> 00:39:10,330
I broke Stannis on the Blackwater.

586
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:12,520
Pity you weren't there to help, Uncle.

587
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:15,290
My apologies, Your Grace. I was rather busy.

588
00:39:15,300 --> 00:39:17,100
Busy getting captured.

589
00:39:18,880 --> 00:39:21,540
So this is the famous "Book of Brothers"?

590
00:39:21,710 --> 00:39:24,410
All the great deeds of all the great Kingsguard.

591
00:39:27,130 --> 00:39:30,780
Ser Arthur Dayne. The Sword of the Morning.

592
00:39:32,990 --> 00:39:35,390
Led the attack on the Kingswood Brotherhood.

593
00:39:35,400 --> 00:39:38,050
Defeated the Smiling Knight in single combat.

594
00:39:39,030 --> 00:39:41,020
Ser Duncan the Tall.

595
00:39:42,940 --> 00:39:44,800
Four pages for Ser Duncan.

596
00:39:45,350 --> 00:39:46,760
He must have been quite a man.

597
00:39:46,760 --> 00:39:48,190
So they say.

598
00:39:51,110 --> 00:39:53,030
Ser Jaime Lannister.

599
00:39:57,290 --> 00:39:59,780
Someone forgot to write down all your great deeds.

600
00:40:00,460 --> 00:40:02,850
-There's still time.  -Is there?

601
00:40:03,180 --> 00:40:06,560
For a 40-year-old knight with one hand?

602
00:40:07,560 --> 00:40:09,960
How can you protect me with that?

603
00:40:09,960 --> 00:40:11,730
I use my left hand now, Your Grace.

604
00:40:11,730 --> 00:40:13,570
Makes for more of a contest.

605
00:40:31,420 --> 00:40:33,030
Have you ever been to Meereen?

606
00:40:33,060 --> 00:40:35,910
Several times, Your Grace, with Master Kraznys.

607
00:40:36,270 --> 00:40:37,410
And?

608
00:40:37,460 --> 00:40:39,440
They say 1,000 slaves died

609
00:40:39,440 --> 00:40:41,310
building the Great Pyramid of Meereen.

610
00:40:41,690 --> 00:40:43,530
And now an army of former slaves

611
00:40:43,530 --> 00:40:45,380
is marching to her gates.

612
00:40:46,820 --> 00:40:48,710
You think the Great Masters are worried?

613
00:40:48,710 --> 00:40:50,920
If they're smart, Your Grace.

614
00:40:54,860 --> 00:40:57,360
You were told to ride at the back of the train.

615
00:40:57,910 --> 00:40:59,410
Yes, my queen.

616
00:40:59,550 --> 00:41:01,780
But I need to speak to you about something important.

617
00:41:02,740 --> 00:41:04,330
A matter of strategy.

618
00:41:08,920 --> 00:41:10,100
Your Grace.

619
00:41:14,080 --> 00:41:16,630
All right, what is this matter of strategy?

620
00:41:19,660 --> 00:41:21,110
A dusk rose.

621
00:41:21,470 --> 00:41:24,170
Would you like to walk at the back of the train instead of riding?

622
00:41:24,430 --> 00:41:27,060
And this one's called Lady's Lace.

623
00:41:27,060 --> 00:41:28,990
Would you like to walk without shoes?

624
00:41:29,600 --> 00:41:31,470
You have to know a land to rule it.

625
00:41:31,470 --> 00:41:33,700
Its plants, its rivers,

626
00:41:33,700 --> 00:41:36,390
its roads, its people.

627
00:41:36,390 --> 00:41:38,520
Dusk rose tea eases fever.

628
00:41:38,520 --> 00:41:40,270
Everyone in Meereen knows that.

629
00:41:40,270 --> 00:41:42,700
Especially the slaves who have to make the tea.

630
00:41:42,860 --> 00:41:44,160
If you want them to follow you,

631
00:41:44,160 --> 00:41:46,020
you have to become a part of their world.

632
00:41:46,080 --> 00:41:47,250
Strategy.

633
00:41:50,460 --> 00:41:51,940
Harpy's Gold.

634
00:41:52,490 --> 00:41:54,100
No tea from this one.

635
00:41:54,100 --> 00:41:55,790
Beautiful, but poisonous.

636
00:42:02,910 --> 00:42:04,970
You are a gambler, aren't you?

637
00:42:12,470 --> 00:42:13,580
Your Grace.

638
00:42:46,270 --> 00:42:49,250
There's one on every mile marker between here and Meereen.

639
00:42:49,630 --> 00:42:52,150
How many miles are there between here and Meereen?

640
00:42:53,000 --> 00:42:55,470
163, Your Grace.

641
00:42:56,100 --> 00:42:58,390
I'll tell our men to ride ahead and bury them.

642
00:42:58,390 --> 00:42:59,720
You don't need to see this.

643
00:42:59,720 --> 00:43:01,370
You will do no such thing.

644
00:43:02,870 --> 00:43:06,580
I will see each and every one of their faces.

645
00:43:08,280 --> 00:43:10,810
Remove her collar before you bury her.

646
00:43:17,970 --> 00:43:19,350
There she is.

647
00:43:19,770 --> 00:43:21,570
Yes, there she is.

648
00:43:23,720 --> 00:43:26,280
-And?  -You made a promise.

649
00:43:26,610 --> 00:43:28,580
To return the Stark girls to their mother

650
00:43:28,580 --> 00:43:29,710
who is now dead.

651
00:43:29,710 --> 00:43:31,280
To keep them safe.

652
00:43:31,280 --> 00:43:34,420
Well, Arya Stark hasn't been seen since her father was killed.

653
00:43:34,420 --> 00:43:35,800
Where do you think she is?

654
00:43:36,040 --> 00:43:37,440
My money's on dead.

655
00:43:37,440 --> 00:43:39,690
There's a certain safety in death, wouldn't you say?

656
00:43:40,180 --> 00:43:43,090
And Sansa Stark is now Sansa Lannister.

657
00:43:43,660 --> 00:43:45,150
Bit of a complication.

658
00:43:45,150 --> 00:43:47,070
A complication does not release you from a vow.

659
00:43:47,070 --> 00:43:49,310
What do you want me to do? Kidnap my sister-in-law?

660
00:43:49,310 --> 00:43:52,410
And take her where? Where would she be safer than here?

661
00:43:52,500 --> 00:43:53,900
Look me in the eye and tell me

662
00:43:53,910 --> 00:43:56,700
that you think she'll be safe in King's Landing.

663
00:44:02,550 --> 00:44:05,700
Are you sure we're not related?

664
00:44:05,700 --> 00:44:07,660
Ever since I've returned, every Lannister I've seen

665
00:44:07,660 --> 00:44:09,530
has been a miserable pain in my ass.

666
00:44:09,530 --> 00:44:11,010
Maybe you're a Lannister, too.

667
00:44:11,080 --> 00:44:13,910
You've got the hair for it if not the looks.

668
00:45:06,150 --> 00:45:07,360
It's all right.

669
00:45:07,370 --> 00:45:09,600
It's all right. It's all right.

670
00:45:11,250 --> 00:45:13,770
-You're drunk.  -Yes.

671
00:45:14,370 --> 00:45:16,180
I have good reason to be.

672
00:45:16,830 --> 00:45:20,370
Once I was a knight. Now I'm only a fool.

673
00:45:22,030 --> 00:45:23,540
Don't you know me?

674
00:45:26,500 --> 00:45:29,480
Ser Dontos. The king's nameday celebration.

675
00:45:29,480 --> 00:45:31,950
I'm sorry. I should have remembered.

676
00:45:31,950 --> 00:45:34,110
I can't accept your apology.

677
00:45:34,110 --> 00:45:37,800
I may be a fool, but I'm a living fool, thanks to you.

678
00:45:38,300 --> 00:45:40,230
Anyone would have done the same.

679
00:45:40,410 --> 00:45:42,100
But only you did.

680
00:45:42,620 --> 00:45:44,400
I can never repay you.

681
00:45:44,430 --> 00:45:45,680
You gave me my life.

682
00:45:46,240 --> 00:45:51,060
But this, this is worth more than my life.

683
00:45:52,950 --> 00:45:56,370
It belonged to my mother and her mother before her.

684
00:45:56,970 --> 00:45:58,870
House Hollard was strong once.

685
00:45:58,880 --> 00:46:00,580
House on the rise.

686
00:46:01,190 --> 00:46:03,160
That's all that's left of those days,

687
00:46:03,200 --> 00:46:06,280
thanks to a few sad, fat drunks like me.

688
00:46:07,250 --> 00:46:09,060
I can't take it.

689
00:46:09,060 --> 00:46:11,860
It's very, very kind of you, but I can't.

690
00:46:11,860 --> 00:46:14,430
I don't have anything else left.

691
00:46:14,770 --> 00:46:16,250
That's all.

692
00:46:16,510 --> 00:46:18,800
Take it. Wear it.

693
00:46:18,800 --> 00:46:20,920
Let my name have one more moment in the sun

694
00:46:20,920 --> 00:46:23,580
before it disappears from the world.

695
00:46:27,730 --> 00:46:30,220
I'll wear it with pride, Ser Dontos.

696
00:46:30,990 --> 00:46:32,230
Yeah.

697
00:46:58,820 --> 00:47:00,790
When am I going to get a horse of my own?

698
00:47:00,790 --> 00:47:02,830
The little lady wants a pony.

699
00:47:03,070 --> 00:47:06,050
The little lady wants away from your stench.

700
00:47:06,060 --> 00:47:08,210
Horses aren't easy to come by.

701
00:47:08,440 --> 00:47:09,680
Even if they were,

702
00:47:09,680 --> 00:47:11,870
you think I'm gonna put you on your own horse?

703
00:47:12,560 --> 00:47:15,840
Watch the only thing of value I've got in the world ride away?

704
00:47:16,790 --> 00:47:18,460
Why don't you have any money?

705
00:47:18,680 --> 00:47:21,430
Didn't you steal anything from Joffrey before you left?

706
00:47:21,580 --> 00:47:22,830
No.

707
00:47:23,420 --> 00:47:25,360
You're not very smart, are you?

708
00:47:25,980 --> 00:47:27,530
I'm not a thief.

709
00:47:27,530 --> 00:47:29,150
You're fine with murdering little boys,

710
00:47:29,150 --> 00:47:31,010
but thieving is beneath you?

711
00:47:31,940 --> 00:47:33,750
A man's got to have a code.

712
00:47:34,070 --> 00:47:36,010
You think I'm gonna escape?

713
00:47:36,860 --> 00:47:38,370
Where would I go?

714
00:47:38,720 --> 00:47:40,100
I'd be dead by nightfall without you.

715
00:47:40,100 --> 00:47:42,780
My family's gone. I've got no one.

716
00:47:44,050 --> 00:47:45,950
You've got an aunt in the Vale.

717
00:47:45,950 --> 00:47:47,520
Your rich Aunt Lysa.

718
00:47:48,100 --> 00:47:49,660
After I sell you to her,

719
00:47:49,810 --> 00:47:51,300
maybe she'll have enough left over

720
00:47:51,300 --> 00:47:53,640
to buy you that pony you want so much.

721
00:47:57,050 --> 00:48:00,140
I'm hungry. You're hungry.

722
00:48:00,140 --> 00:48:02,360
Five horses, five men.

723
00:48:02,880 --> 00:48:06,030
More than I feel like killing on an empty stomach.

724
00:48:13,270 --> 00:48:14,580
I know him.

725
00:48:15,060 --> 00:48:17,900
The small one. His name is Polliver.

726
00:48:18,090 --> 00:48:20,460
He captured us and took us to Harrenhal.

727
00:48:22,750 --> 00:48:24,280
He killed Lommy.

728
00:48:25,030 --> 00:48:26,700
What the fuck's a Lommy?

729
00:48:26,700 --> 00:48:28,310
He was my friend.

730
00:48:29,320 --> 00:48:32,360
Polliver stole my sword and put it right through his neck.

731
00:48:34,680 --> 00:48:35,970
He's still got it.

732
00:48:36,010 --> 00:48:37,340
Got what?

733
00:48:37,350 --> 00:48:39,560
My sword, Needle.

734
00:48:39,570 --> 00:48:42,990
Needle? Of course you named your sword.

735
00:48:42,990 --> 00:48:44,840
Lots of people name their swords.

736
00:48:44,840 --> 00:48:46,620
Lots of cunts.

737
00:48:52,630 --> 00:48:54,210
What are you? Get back here.

738
00:48:54,210 --> 00:48:55,930
My brother gave me that sword.

739
00:48:56,350 --> 00:48:58,740
-Get back here.  -He killed my friend.

740
00:48:58,880 --> 00:49:00,950
I don't care if he ate your friend.

741
00:49:00,950 --> 00:49:02,380
We're not going in there.

742
00:49:06,650 --> 00:49:08,530
Come on, give it up.

743
00:49:13,310 --> 00:49:14,640
Come here.

744
00:49:15,580 --> 00:49:18,130
-Let's have a feel there.  -Leave it.

745
00:49:48,810 --> 00:49:50,020
Come here.

746
00:49:51,810 --> 00:49:53,390
Please, she's a good girl.

747
00:49:53,390 --> 00:49:55,190
Shut your mouth and pour us more ale

748
00:49:55,190 --> 00:49:57,460
and we may not take her with us when we're done with her.

749
00:50:02,700 --> 00:50:04,040
I know you.

750
00:50:07,270 --> 00:50:08,640
You're the Hound.

751
00:50:11,000 --> 00:50:12,700
Pour our new friend some ale.

752
00:50:17,540 --> 00:50:19,310
What brings you so far north?

753
00:50:19,310 --> 00:50:21,190
I could ask the same of you.

754
00:50:21,260 --> 00:50:22,570
What are you doing up here?

755
00:50:22,570 --> 00:50:24,090
Just keeping the king's peace.

756
00:50:24,090 --> 00:50:25,920
No need. The war's over.

757
00:50:25,920 --> 00:50:29,130
So I've heard. Stannis defeated at the Blackwater.

758
00:50:29,140 --> 00:50:31,000
Robb Stark killed at the Twins.

759
00:50:31,000 --> 00:50:32,660
And where am I for all of it?

760
00:50:32,690 --> 00:50:34,350
Stuck with your brother.

761
00:50:34,840 --> 00:50:37,250
-Meaning no offense.  -None taken.

762
00:50:37,250 --> 00:50:38,970
He's good, the Mountain is.

763
00:50:38,970 --> 00:50:40,300
Best at what he does.

764
00:50:40,300 --> 00:50:44,110
But torture, torture, torture, torture.

765
00:50:44,260 --> 00:50:46,560
You spend enough time putting the hammer to people,

766
00:50:46,560 --> 00:50:49,590
you start to feel like a carpenter making chairs.

767
00:50:49,590 --> 00:50:51,460
Drains the fun right out of it.

768
00:50:51,460 --> 00:50:53,270
And what's life without a little fun?

769
00:50:56,550 --> 00:50:58,600
But I don't need to tell you that, eh?

770
00:51:00,810 --> 00:51:03,550
She's all right. I've had better.

771
00:51:06,700 --> 00:51:07,900
You know what?

772
00:51:09,160 --> 00:51:10,700
You should come with us.

773
00:51:11,660 --> 00:51:14,830
His kind, they've always got something hidden away somewhere.

774
00:51:14,830 --> 00:51:17,750
Gold, silver, more daughters.

775
00:51:17,750 --> 00:51:20,200
Always something if you know how to make them talk.

776
00:51:20,200 --> 00:51:22,690
And there's plenty of him between here and King's Landing.

777
00:51:22,800 --> 00:51:24,420
You could do well for yourself.

778
00:51:24,420 --> 00:51:25,940
We certainly have been.

779
00:51:29,780 --> 00:51:31,930
I'm not going to King's Landing.

780
00:51:31,990 --> 00:51:34,290
Think about it. We could do whatever we like

781
00:51:34,290 --> 00:51:35,750
wherever we go.

782
00:51:37,450 --> 00:51:39,320
These are the king's colors.

783
00:51:39,510 --> 00:51:41,620
No one's standing in his way now.

784
00:51:41,620 --> 00:51:43,950
Which means no one's standing in ours.

785
00:51:46,180 --> 00:51:47,760
Fuck the king.

786
00:51:58,020 --> 00:52:00,150
When I heard that Joffrey's dog had tucked tail

787
00:52:00,150 --> 00:52:02,320
and run from the Battle of the Blackwater,

788
00:52:02,320 --> 00:52:04,000
I didn't believe it.

789
00:52:04,420 --> 00:52:06,500
-But here you are.  -Here I am.

790
00:52:07,560 --> 00:52:09,720
Bring me one of those chickens.

791
00:52:09,720 --> 00:52:12,390
-You got money to pay for it?  -You paid for it?

792
00:52:13,060 --> 00:52:14,090
No.

793
00:52:14,720 --> 00:52:16,380
But we're the king's men.

794
00:52:17,060 --> 00:52:19,760
So, you got money?

795
00:52:20,030 --> 00:52:21,640
Not a penny.

796
00:52:22,030 --> 00:52:24,300
I'll still take that chicken.

797
00:52:24,620 --> 00:52:25,860
Tell you what.

798
00:52:26,410 --> 00:52:27,930
We'll trade you.

799
00:52:27,990 --> 00:52:30,740
One of our little chickens for one of yours.

800
00:52:31,450 --> 00:52:33,200
Give us a go at your friend.

801
00:52:34,530 --> 00:52:37,490
Lowell there likes them a bit broken in.

802
00:52:44,390 --> 00:52:46,020
You're a talker.

803
00:52:47,770 --> 00:52:51,280
Listening to talkers makes me thirsty.

804
00:53:08,840 --> 00:53:10,460
And hungry.

805
00:53:11,080 --> 00:53:13,310
Think I'll take two chickens.

806
00:53:22,380 --> 00:53:24,690
You don't seem to understand the situation.

807
00:53:25,150 --> 00:53:27,250
I understand that if any more words

808
00:53:27,250 --> 00:53:29,650
come pouring out of your cunt mouth,

809
00:53:30,500 --> 00:53:33,910
I'm gonna have to eat every fucking chicken in this room.

810
00:53:34,790 --> 00:53:36,720
You lived your life for the king.

811
00:53:38,280 --> 00:53:40,280
You're gonna die for some chickens?

812
00:53:41,510 --> 00:53:43,080
Someone is.

813
00:55:40,950 --> 00:55:43,000
Something wrong with your leg, boy?

814
00:55:43,360 --> 00:55:45,810
What? What do you mean?

815
00:55:45,810 --> 00:55:49,350
Can you walk? I've got to carry you?

816
00:55:49,650 --> 00:55:51,230
Carry me?

817
00:55:53,100 --> 00:55:54,660
Fine little blade.

818
00:56:00,400 --> 00:56:02,520
Maybe I'll pick my teeth with it.

